00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
One of my favourite TV series is Mad Men. Set in the advertising world of the

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.260
1960s, it's a world of smoky boardrooms, hard-drinking and the craft of writing

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.100
persuasive adverts. One of the main characters is Roger Sterling, charismatic

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.740
silver-haired, razor-sharp partner and head of accounts, always ready with

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.100
witty one-liners. Now he's not the creative genius like Don Draper, he has

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.220
an instinct for what lands and how to keep highly erratic clients happy. Now in

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.060
one scene, the creative team are really struggling to land the right idea and

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:36.580
Sterling quips, "I'll tell you what brilliance in advertising is. 99 cents."

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:41.800
Somebody thought of that. It's such a simple line, 99 cents, somebody thought of

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.660
that, but it says a lot, right? Until someone thought of that, everything was

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.820
priced around that price point at a dollar. Straight, round, quite plain. Then

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:58.160
someone thought of 99 cents and then the whole world shifted. Here's why. 99p

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.900
feels different to one pound. 149 feels different to 150. The difference is

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.420
negligible and we know it but the feeling isn't. One catches your eye, it

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.940
makes you pause and the key is people aren't fooled. They know it's basically

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.200
the same but it's something about the presentation. It's clever without being

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.000
dishonest and that's the key point. Presentation really matters. It always has,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.740
it always will. Now advertising people write copy. They script slogans and print

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:31.600
posters but as a consultant you are on the front line of advertising yourself,

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.060
your ideas, your company. Every client conversation, every recommendation, every

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.860
email and every meeting, that's your advert. The words you choose to use shape

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.340
what people think of you and how they experience you and whether they're

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.580
compelled by what you say and whether they believe what you say. In a world of

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:54.720
clichés and over-elaboration, particularly now in the world of AI, we

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.260
should continuously ask ourselves what's the simplest way you can say what you do?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:05.740
What's the clearest way you can describe the impact that your company can make? Too

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.980
often we bury it in absolute nonsense. Imagine saying we are cutting-edge

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.020
provider of human-centric performance enablement solutions that synergise

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.700
behavioural insight with commercial outcomes. That's a real advert by the way.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.340
Or you could just say what you actually do in plain words that a real human

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.220
being would use and under that simplicity of course sits the fuller

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:33.260
story. All the honesty, the rigour and the craft, but the simple line is a door

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:40.500
people want to walk through, to work with you. 99p is so simple. A single penny

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.380
changed the way the world priced things, not by tricking anyone but by presenting

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:52.000
value in a way that people simply enjoyed. For a consultant that kind of

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.980
clarity and communication is a great way to engage your client. Your client is

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:02.700
busy, normally sceptical and pulled in how many directions. The consultant who can

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:08.580
say what they do or what their idea is in a clean and simple authentic human

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:14.260
line is far easier to trust and far easier to champion in a room that you're

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:20.180
not even in. Your version of 99p is not a trick. It is simply respect for a

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.260
client's time and for their attention.
